---
// <BcnBoundaryDrawMap> — an EDITABLE Leaflet map for capturing a project boundary.
// The user either DRAWS the site outline (polygon or rectangle, then edits or deletes
// it) or UPLOADS a GIS file; either way the component measures the resulting shape and
// ANNOUNCES it. It is the input half of the "Define project boundary" due-diligence
// step; it renders no summary card, no project form, and no Continue button.
//
// DUMB ON PURPOSE, the same contract BcnObservationMap keeps: this component owns the
// basemap, the draw toolbar, the basemap picker, the upload zone and the measurement,
// and nothing else. Every create / edit / delete dispatches ONE bubbling event on the
// root —
//
//   bcn-boundary-change
//     detail = {
//       vertices:    number,           // ring vertices, excluding the closing point
//       perimeterKm: number,           // 2dp
//       perimeterFt: number,           // 0dp
//       acres:       number,           // 1dp
//       areaSqm:     number,           // 0dp
//       centroid:    { lat, lon },     // 5dp — bounds centre, see MEASUREMENT below
//       source:      'draw' | 'upload' // additive: lets a host caption "from file"
//       fileName?:   string            // additive: present when source === 'upload'
//     }
//     detail = null  ⟵  the boundary was DELETED. The host hides its summary.
//
// — so the HOST decides whether that fills a summary card, unlocks Continue, or writes
// a jurisdiction field. That is what makes the component safe to mount twice on a page.
//
// MEASUREMENT is deliberately approximate and says so. Perimeter is a real haversine
// walk of the ring (Leaflet's distanceTo). Area prefers L.GeometryUtil.geodesicArea,
// which Leaflet.draw ships, and falls back to a cos(lat)-scaled shoelace. The centroid
// is the BOUNDS centre, not the polygon's true centroid — for a site outline the two
// are within metres of each other and the bounds centre is what the surface it replaces
// showed. None of this is survey-grade; a real boundary arrives from the uploaded file
// once the spatial-data epic lands, and this is the prototype standing in for it.
//
// THE UPLOAD IS SIMULATED, exactly as the pre-design-system prototype at
// public/due-diligence/due-diligence/new-project.html simulated it: picking any file
// re-seeds the demo boundary and fires the same event with `source: 'upload'`. Nothing
// is parsed. When no `seedRing` was supplied there is no demo shape to re-seed, so the
// ring is derived from the CURRENT map view (inset 25%) — deterministic, credible, and
// it invents no coordinates the caller did not already choose by framing the map.
//
// MULTI-INSTANCE CONTRACT — an Astro `<script>` is hoisted and bundled ONCE per page,
// not re-run per instance, so props are NOT visible to it as a closure. Every DOM id is
// namespaced by the REQUIRED `idPrefix`, and props are threaded through the DOM instead:
// `data-*` on the root plus a sibling `<script type="application/json"
// data-bcn-bmap-data={idPrefix}>` payload. The module walks every `[data-bcn-bmap]` and
// builds an independent map per root. Same idiom as BcnFootprintMap / BcnObservationMap.
//
// Leaflet gotchas, inherited from the siblings and one of this component's own:
//   1. `setView()` must run BEFORE any layer is added, or Leaflet throws on the first
//      tile. fitBounds to the seed ring then takes over.
//   3. a map built in a 0×0 container fits against nothing and opens over the ocean.
//      This one may mount in a two-column step layout that is still settling, so it
//      DEFERS construction until its box has real size and then re-fits once more via
//      ResizeObserver — the caller never has to poke it on reveal.
//   4. (new) Leaflet.draw 1.0.4 predates Leaflet 1.7's touch refactor and its UMD
//      bundle reads the GLOBAL `L` rather than requiring 'leaflet'. Both are handled at
//      the top of boot() — see the comments there.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: Ecology has no map, geo, spatial or draw lego at all — `ls
// node_modules/@esa/ecology/src/components/` (verified against the live symlinked hub
// source) has nothing of the kind, and the hub's /components esa-map entry is a doc
// page with no source behind it. Checked Beacon prod: its map is an Angular/Leaflet
// page, not a reusable ui-* control, and it has no boundary-drawing surface. Both
// sibling maps were read in full and NEITHER can be reused: BcnFootprintMap and
// BcnObservationMap are DISPLAY-ONLY — they take finished geometry as a prop and plot
// it, have no editable layer, no draw/edit/delete handlers and no way to emit a shape
// back out, so extending either into an editor would fork their display contract for
// every existing caller. This is the reusable home for an EDITABLE boundary. Every
// control AROUND the map is a lego and is used as one: the method switch IS
// esa-button-toggle, the basemap picker IS esa-select, the upload zone IS
// esa-file-upload (no hand-rolled dropzone). The drawing itself is the standard,
// widely-used MIT-licensed Leaflet.draw plugin, not a bespoke reinvention. The CSS
// below is the map container's own geometry plus a restyle of the toolbar Leaflet
// injects into its own panes — DOM no lego can reach, the same reason
// styles/beacon-map.css exists.
import '../../styles/beacon-map.css';

interface Props {
  /** Namespaces every DOM id so two instances can coexist. REQUIRED — no singletons. */
  idPrefix: string;
  /** Optional closed ring of [lat, lon] pairs, drawn as the initial EDITABLE shape so
   *  the component demonstrates a wired-up state out of the box. Also the shape the
   *  simulated upload re-seeds. */
  seedRing?: [number, number][];
  /** CSS height of the map surface. A fixed frame that never resizes on interaction. */
  height?: string;
  /** Names the map for assistive tech. NOT rendered as a heading — the host owns the
   *  step's heading hierarchy (same call BcnFootprintMap's full variant makes). */
  title?: string;
}

const {
  idPrefix,
  seedRing = [],
  height = '560px',
  title = 'Project boundary',
} = Astro.props;

const payload = { seedRing };

const mapId = `${idPrefix}-map`;
const methodId = `${idPrefix}-method`;
const basemapId = `${idPrefix}-basemap`;
const uploadId = `${idPrefix}-upload`;
const hintId = `${idPrefix}-hint`;

const mapLabel = `${title} — draw or edit the site outline`;
---

<div class="bcn-bmap" id={`${idPrefix}-root`} data-bcn-bmap data-prefix={idPrefix}>
  <div class="stack" data-gap="md">
    {/* Method switch left, basemap picker right — both legos, no bespoke buttons. */}
    <div class="repel bcn-bmap__bar" data-gap="md">
      <esa-button-toggle id={methodId} size="sm" label="Boundary method"></esa-button-toggle>
      <esa-select id={basemapId} size="sm" label="Basemap"></esa-select>
    </div>

    <div
      class="bcn-bmap__surface"
      id={mapId}
      style={`height: ${height};`}
      role="region"
      aria-label={mapLabel}
    >
    </div>

    {/* Draw mode: one line naming the tools, because a toolbar of Leaflet glyphs does
        not say "closed shapes only" on its own. */}
    <p class="bcn-bmap__hint" id={hintId}>
      Use the polygon or rectangle tool on the map to trace the site outline, then the
      edit tool to move a vertex. A boundary is a closed shape — points and lines are off.
    </p>

    {/* Upload mode. A caller may replace the whole zone via the slot; the fallback is
        the real esa-file-upload lego. Either way the panel listens for the bubbling
        `change` a file control emits, so a slotted esa-file-upload wires itself. */}
    <div class="bcn-bmap__upload" id={uploadId} hidden>
      <slot name="upload">
        <esa-file-upload
          label="Upload a GIS file"
          accept=".zip,.geojson,.json,.kml,.kmz"
          name="boundary-file"></esa-file-upload>
      </slot>
      <p class="bcn-bmap__hint">
        Shapefile (.zip), GeoJSON, or KML/KMZ. Prototype: the file is not parsed — selecting
        one loads the demo boundary so the rest of the step can be reviewed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script
  type="application/json"
  data-bcn-bmap-data={idPrefix}
  set:html={JSON.stringify(payload)}
></script>

<script>
  import L from 'leaflet';
  import 'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css';
  import 'leaflet-draw/dist/leaflet.draw.css';
  import { BASEMAP_TILE_URL, BASEMAP_ATTRIBUTION } from '../../lib/basemap';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-button-toggle';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-select';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-file-upload';

  type BmapRoot = HTMLElement & {
    _bcnBmapReady?: boolean;
    /** Host handle: the live Leaflet map, for a caller that needs to fly somewhere. */
    _bcnMap?: L.Map;
    /** Host handle: re-seed the demo boundary programmatically (what a slotted upload
     *  control would call if it wanted to trigger the simulation itself). */
    _bcnSeedBoundary?: (fileName?: string) => void;
  };

  type ToggleEl = HTMLElement & { options: unknown[]; value: string };
  type SelectEl = HTMLElement & { options: unknown[]; value: string };

  /** Statewide California — the neutral view when there is no seed to fit. */
  const EMPTY_VIEW: [number, number] = [37.6, -120.4];
  const EMPTY_ZOOM = 5;
  const DRAW_FALLBACK = '#005862';
  const SQM_PER_ACRE = 4046.86;
  const M_PER_FT = 3.28084;

  const rootStyle = () => getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);

  /**
   * Leaflet paths take LITERAL colors, so a `var(--color-background-brand)` has to be resolved
   * first. Recurses because a semantic token may alias another var(), and honors an
   * inline var() fallback. Lifted verbatim from BcnFootprintMap / BcnObservationMap —
   * the third map to need it, and the reason it reads the same in all three.
   */
  function resolveColor(value: string, depth = 0): string {
    const raw = (value || '').trim();
    if (!raw || depth > 4) return DRAW_FALLBACK;
    const m = raw.match(/^var\(\s*(--[\w-]+)\s*(?:,\s*([\s\S]+))?\)$/);
    if (!m) return raw;
    const resolved = rootStyle().getPropertyValue(m[1]).trim();
    if (resolved) return resolveColor(resolved, depth + 1);
    return m[2] ? resolveColor(m[2], depth + 1) : DRAW_FALLBACK;
  }

  /**
   * Streets is the shared Mapbox Light sheet every map in the spoke uses (src/lib/
   * basemap.ts), not the full-color OSM one: house rule is that the container stays
   * neutral so the drawn boundary carries the only color. Satellite and Terrain are
   * the two cases where the imagery IS the information — you cannot trace a site
   * outline against a gray rectangle.
   */
  const BASEMAPS: Record<string, () => L.TileLayer> = {
    streets: () => L.tileLayer(BASEMAP_TILE_URL, { attribution: BASEMAP_ATTRIBUTION, maxZoom: 19 }),
    satellite: () =>
      L.tileLayer(
        'https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer/tile/{z}/{y}/{x}',
        { attribution: '&copy; Esri World Imagery', maxZoom: 19 },
      ),
    terrain: () =>
      L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.opentopomap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', {
        attribution: '&copy; OpenTopoMap',
        maxZoom: 17,
      }),
  };

  const BASEMAP_OPTIONS = [
    { label: 'Streets', value: 'streets' },
    { label: 'Satellite', value: 'satellite' },
    { label: 'Terrain', value: 'terrain' },
  ];

  const METHOD_OPTIONS = [
    { label: 'Draw on map', value: 'draw' },
    { label: 'Upload file', value: 'upload' },
  ];

  function readSeed(prefix: string): [number, number][] {
    const el = document.querySelector(`[data-bcn-bmap-data="${prefix}"]`);
    if (!el) return [];
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(el.textContent || 'null');
      const ring = parsed?.seedRing;
      return Array.isArray(ring) ? (ring as [number, number][]) : [];
    } catch {
      return [];
    }
  }

  /** The ring a polygon or a rectangle carries — both nest one level. */
  function ringOf(layer: L.Polygon): L.LatLng[] {
    const raw = layer.getLatLngs() as L.LatLng[] | L.LatLng[][];
    return Array.isArray(raw[0]) ? (raw[0] as L.LatLng[]) : (raw as L.LatLng[]);
  }

  /**
   * cos(lat)-scaled shoelace — the fallback when Leaflet.draw's GeometryUtil is absent.
   * Good to a percent or two at site scale, which is all a prototype summary needs.
   */
  function shoelaceSqm(ring: L.LatLng[]): number {
    let s = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < ring.length; i++) {
      const a = ring[i];
      const b = ring[(i + 1) % ring.length];
      s += (b.lng - a.lng) * (b.lat + a.lat);
    }
    const mPerDeg = 111319.9;
    return Math.abs(s) * 0.5 * mPerDeg * mPerDeg * Math.cos((ring[0].lat * Math.PI) / 180);
  }

  interface BoundaryDetail {
    vertices: number;
    perimeterKm: number;
    perimeterFt: number;
    acres: number;
    areaSqm: number;
    centroid: { lat: number; lon: number };
    source: 'draw' | 'upload';
    fileName?: string;
  }

  const round = (n: number, places: number) => Number(n.toFixed(places));

  /** Measure a drawn shape into the event's detail shape. */
  function measure(
    layer: L.Polygon,
    source: 'draw' | 'upload',
    fileName?: string,
  ): BoundaryDetail | null {
    const ring = ringOf(layer);
    if (ring.length < 3) return null;

    let perimeterM = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < ring.length; i++) {
      perimeterM += ring[i].distanceTo(ring[(i + 1) % ring.length]);
    }

    // Leaflet.draw ships L.GeometryUtil.geodesicArea; prefer it, fall back to shoelace.
    const geodesic = (L as unknown as { GeometryUtil?: { geodesicArea?: (r: L.LatLng[]) => number } })
      .GeometryUtil?.geodesicArea;
    const areaSqm =
      typeof geodesic === 'function' ? Math.abs(geodesic(ring)) : shoelaceSqm(ring);

    const centre = layer.getBounds().getCenter();

    return {
      vertices: ring.length,
      perimeterKm: round(perimeterM / 1000, 2),
      perimeterFt: round(perimeterM * M_PER_FT, 0),
      acres: round(areaSqm / SQM_PER_ACRE, 1),
      areaSqm: round(areaSqm, 0),
      centroid: { lat: round(centre.lat, 5), lon: round(centre.lng, 5) },
      source,
      ...(fileName ? { fileName } : {}),
    };
  }

  function build(root: BmapRoot) {
    if (root._bcnBmapReady) return;
    root._bcnBmapReady = true;

    const prefix = root.dataset.prefix || '';
    const mapEl = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-map`);
    if (!mapEl) return;

    const seedRing = readSeed(prefix);
    const drawColor = resolveColor('var(--color-background-brand)');
    const shapeOptions: L.PolylineOptions = {
      color: drawColor,
      weight: 2,
      fillColor: drawColor,
      fillOpacity: 0.15,
    };

    // Gotcha 1: a view must exist BEFORE any layer is added.
    const map = L.map(mapEl, { zoomControl: true, attributionControl: true }).setView(
      EMPTY_VIEW,
      EMPTY_ZOOM,
    );

    let base = BASEMAPS.streets().addTo(map);

    // ── Boundary layer: exactly ONE shape lives here, ever ──
    const drawn = new L.FeatureGroup();
    map.addLayer(drawn);

    const announce = (detail: BoundaryDetail | null) => {
      root.dispatchEvent(
        new CustomEvent('bcn-boundary-change', { detail, bubbles: true }),
      );
    };

    /** Replace whatever is drawn with `layer`, measure it, announce it, frame it. */
    function adopt(layer: L.Polygon, source: 'draw' | 'upload', fileName?: string) {
      drawn.clearLayers();
      layer.setStyle(shapeOptions);
      drawn.addLayer(layer);
      const bounds = layer.getBounds();
      if (bounds.isValid()) map.fitBounds(bounds, { padding: [40, 40], maxZoom: 17 });
      announce(measure(layer, source, fileName));
    }

    /**
     * The shape the simulated upload produces: the seed ring when the caller gave one,
     * otherwise the current view inset 25% — deterministic, and it invents no
     * coordinates the caller did not already pick by framing the map.
     */
    function demoRing(): [number, number][] {
      if (seedRing.length >= 3) return seedRing;
      const b = map.getBounds();
      const dLat = (b.getNorth() - b.getSouth()) * 0.25;
      const dLng = (b.getEast() - b.getWest()) * 0.25;
      const s = b.getSouth() + dLat;
      const n = b.getNorth() - dLat;
      const w = b.getWest() + dLng;
      const e = b.getEast() - dLng;
      return [
        [s, w],
        [s, e],
        [n, e],
        [n, w],
      ];
    }

    const seedBoundary = (fileName?: string) => {
      adopt(
        L.polygon(demoRing() as L.LatLngExpression[], shapeOptions),
        fileName ? 'upload' : 'draw',
        fileName,
      );
    };

    // ── Draw toolbar: closed shapes only. No markers, circles, or polylines — a
    //    boundary that is not closed is not a boundary. `showArea` stays off because
    //    Leaflet.draw 1.0.4's readableArea throws on non-metric units. ──
    const drawControl = new L.Control.Draw({
      position: 'topleft',
      edit: { featureGroup: drawn, remove: true },
      draw: {
        polyline: false,
        marker: false,
        circle: false,
        circlemarker: false,
        polygon: { shapeOptions, showArea: false, allowIntersection: false },
        rectangle: { shapeOptions, showArea: false },
      },
    } as L.Control.DrawConstructorOptions);
    map.addControl(drawControl);

    map.on(L.Draw.Event.CREATED, (e) => {
      adopt((e as L.DrawEvents.Created).layer as L.Polygon, 'draw');
    });
    map.on(L.Draw.Event.EDITED, (e) => {
      (e as L.DrawEvents.Edited).layers.eachLayer((layer) => {
        announce(measure(layer as L.Polygon, 'draw'));
      });
    });
    map.on(L.Draw.Event.DELETED, () => {
      // One shape at a time, so a delete empties the group and the host hides its card.
      const left = drawn.getLayers();
      if (left.length === 0) announce(null);
      else announce(measure(left[0] as L.Polygon, 'draw'));
    });

    // ── Method switch (esa-button-toggle) ──
    const method = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-method`) as ToggleEl | null;
    const uploadPanel = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-upload`);
    const hint = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-hint`);
    if (method) {
      method.options = METHOD_OPTIONS;
      method.value = 'draw';
      method.addEventListener('change', (ev) => {
        const value = (ev as CustomEvent<{ value: string }>).detail?.value;
        const drawing = value !== 'upload';
        if (uploadPanel) uploadPanel.hidden = drawing;
        if (hint) hint.hidden = !drawing;
        // The toolbar is removed in upload mode rather than left as dead chrome:
        // two live ways to set one boundary is a question the step never asks.
        if (drawing) map.addControl(drawControl);
        else map.removeControl(drawControl);
      });
    }

    // ── Basemap picker (esa-select) ──
    const basemap = document.getElementById(`${prefix}-basemap`) as SelectEl | null;
    if (basemap) {
      basemap.options = BASEMAP_OPTIONS;
      basemap.value = 'streets';
      basemap.addEventListener('change', (ev) => {
        const value = (ev as CustomEvent<{ value: string }>).detail?.value || 'streets';
        const next = (BASEMAPS[value] || BASEMAPS.streets)();
        map.removeLayer(base);
        base = next.addTo(map);
        base.bringToBack();
      });
    }

    // ── Upload path (esa-file-upload, or whatever the caller slotted in its place).
    //    The lego's `change` bubbles and is composed, so one listener on the panel
    //    catches the fallback AND a slotted replacement. ──
    if (uploadPanel) {
      uploadPanel.addEventListener('change', (ev) => {
        const files = (ev as CustomEvent<{ files?: File[] }>).detail?.files;
        if (!Array.isArray(files) || files.length === 0) return;
        seedBoundary(files[0].name);
      });
    }

    // Seed LAST, so the initial shape is framed after the basemap and toolbar exist.
    if (seedRing.length >= 3) {
      adopt(L.polygon(seedRing as L.LatLngExpression[], shapeOptions), 'draw');
    }

    // Gotcha 3, second half: a container that gains size after boot (two-column step
    // layout still settling, a revealed panel) re-measures and re-frames once.
    requestAnimationFrame(() => map.invalidateSize());
    if (typeof ResizeObserver !== 'undefined') {
      let settled = mapEl.clientWidth > 0 && mapEl.clientHeight > 0;
      const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {
        if (settled || mapEl.clientWidth === 0 || mapEl.clientHeight === 0) return;
        settled = true;
        map.invalidateSize();
        const b = drawn.getBounds();
        if (b.isValid()) map.fitBounds(b, { padding: [40, 40], maxZoom: 17 });
        ro.disconnect();
      });
      ro.observe(mapEl);
    }

    root._bcnMap = map;
    root._bcnSeedBoundary = seedBoundary;
  }

  async function boot() {
    // Gotcha 4a: leaflet-draw 1.0.4's UMD bundle is `!function(w,d){ L.Draw = … }`
    // — it reads the GLOBAL `L` and never requires 'leaflet'. So the global has to
    // exist BEFORE the module evaluates, which a static import cannot guarantee
    // (imports hoist above assignments). Hence assign, then dynamic-import.
    (window as unknown as { L: typeof L }).L = L;
    await import('leaflet-draw');

    // Gotcha 4b: the same 1.0.4 predates Leaflet 1.7's touch refactor and its
    // _onTouch reaches for an event shape that no longer exists, throwing mid-draw
    // on pen/touch input. Upstream Leaflet.draw#1026 — neutralise the handler.
    (L as unknown as { Draw: { Polyline: { prototype: Record<string, unknown> } } }).Draw
      .Polyline.prototype._onTouch = L.Util.falseFn;

    // Gotcha 3, first half: build LAZILY once the box has real size. A map created in
    // a 0×0 container fits against nothing and opens over the middle of the ocean.
    document.querySelectorAll<BmapRoot>('[data-bcn-bmap]').forEach((root) => {
      const el = document.getElementById(`${root.dataset.prefix || ''}-map`);
      if (!el) return;
      if (el.clientWidth > 0 && el.clientHeight > 0) {
        build(root);
        return;
      }
      if (typeof ResizeObserver === 'undefined') {
        build(root);
        return;
      }
      const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {
        if (el.clientWidth === 0 || el.clientHeight === 0) return;
        ro.disconnect();
        build(root);
      });
      ro.observe(el);
    });
  }

  void boot();
</script>

<style>
  /* Controls row: the two legos carry their own labels, so they align on their
     CONTROL baselines, not their box tops. Wraps before it squeezes either one.
     position+z-index is load-bearing, not decoration: Leaflet's own panes
     (.leaflet-top/.leaflet-control-container etc.) sit at z-index 1000, and
     .bcn-bmap__surface's UA-positioned .leaflet-container never establishes its
     OWN stacking context (position:relative with no z-index), so those pane
     z-indices escape upward and paint over any later sibling with a lower
     z-index — which is every popover a lego opens from this bar. Without this,
     the basemap esa-select's dropdown genuinely opens (confirmed in devtools)
     but renders invisible behind the map. */
  .bcn-bmap__bar {
    align-items: flex-end;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1200;
  }

  /* Map-container geometry only — rounded, clipped, sunken while tiles load. The exact
     treatment BcnFootprintMap's .bcn-fmap__surface and BcnObservationMap give theirs,
     so every map in the spoke reads as the same object. Height is the `height` prop. */
  .bcn-bmap__surface {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius-200);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken);
  }

  /* Leaflet injects .leaflet-container itself, so it is outside Astro's scope. */
  .bcn-bmap__surface :global(.leaflet-container) {
    font-family: var(--typography-font-family-sans, inherit);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken);
  }
  /* An editable map offers a crosshair while a draw handler is armed — Leaflet.draw
     sets this class on the container, and its own default is a dotted cursor URL. */
  .bcn-bmap__surface :global(.leaflet-container.leaflet-crosshair) {
    cursor: crosshair;
  }

  /* Leaflet.draw's toolbar is injected into Leaflet's own control pane, so no lego and
     no component scope can reach it. Bring it to the house control language: the 4px
     control radius, semantic surface and border. Glyphs stay the plugin's sprite. */
  .bcn-bmap__surface :global(.leaflet-draw-toolbar a) {
    background-color: var(--color-background-elevation-raised);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-border-default);
  }
  .bcn-bmap__surface :global(.leaflet-draw-toolbar a:hover) {
    background-color: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken);
  }
  .bcn-bmap__surface :global(.leaflet-bar) {
    border-radius: var(--radius-100);
